# 10. Branches & Variations

## Weighted KNN

Instead of giving every neighbor equal importance:

```text
Closer neighbor → Higher importance
Farther neighbor → Lower importance
```

A common idea is:

\[
Weight=\frac{1}{Distance}
\]

This can improve local predictions.

---

## Radius Neighbors

Instead of choosing exactly K neighbors:

> Select every point within a certain radius.

Useful when data density varies.

---

## Approximate Nearest Neighbors

For large-scale applications, approximate methods can find similar points faster than exact brute-force search.

Common modern use cases include searching through large embedding collections.

